Notebook[{Cell["InfraCausality", "GuideTitle"], 
  Cell["InfraCausality contains fundamental constructions on finite directed \
acyclic graphs. Vertices represent events, and reachability defines their \
causal order: an event precedes another when a directed path connects them. \
Including equality makes this relation a partial order. Chains consist of \
comparable events, while antichains consist of mutually incomparable events. \
The order also defines a topology whose open sets are upward closed: \
containing an event requires containing its causal future.", 
   "GuideAbstract"], Cell["A worldline is a saturated chain: no event can be \
inserted between consecutive members. A longest chain between two events is \
the discrete model used here for a timelike geodesic. The discrete light-cone \
construction retains events whose causal interval with the anchor is itself a \
chain. These are combinatorial definitions; recovering classical relativistic \
geometry requires further assumptions.", "GuideAbstract"], 
  Cell["Causal height counts the edges of a longest chain from a source to an \
event. Its level sets are antichains, but need not meet every maximal causal \
path. Spatial reconstruction and comparison between slices are discussed in \
InfraSubstrates.", "GuideAbstract"], Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection"], 
  Cell["Causal order and intervals", "GuideFunctionsSubsection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraChainQ", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] tests an ordered chain in the reachability order"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraAntichainQ", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] tests a set of mutually incomparable events"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraCausalFuture", "InlineCode"], 
     ", ", StyleBox["InfraCausalPast", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] the future and past of an event or event set"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraCausalDiamond", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] the causal interval between two events"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraCausalFutureQ", "InlineCode"], ", ", 
     StyleBox["InfraCausalPastQ", "InlineCode"], ", ", 
     StyleBox["InfraCausalDiamondQ", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] recognize the corresponding event sets"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell["Worldlines and discrete relativistic geometry", 
   "GuideFunctionsSubsection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraWorldline", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] the family of saturated chains between events"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraTimelikeGeodesic", 
      "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] the family of longest chains between events"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraFutureLightCone", 
      "InlineCode"], ", ", StyleBox["InfraPastLightCone", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] the discrete light cones defined by chain intervals"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["RandomInfraWorldline", 
      "InlineCode"], ", ", StyleBox["RandomInfraTimelikeGeodesic", 
      "InlineCode"], " \[LongDash] sample saturated or longest chains"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["RandomInfraFutureLightCone", 
      "InlineCode"], ", ", StyleBox["RandomInfraPastLightCone", 
      "InlineCode"], " \[LongDash] sample light rays"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraWorldlineQ", "InlineCode"], ", ", 
     StyleBox["InfraTimelikeGeodesicQ", "InlineCode"], ", ", 
     StyleBox["InfraLightRayQ", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] test individual chains"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell["Time and slices", "GuideFunctionsSubsection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["CausalHeight", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] the longest-chain length from a source to each event"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["CausalHeightFoliation", 
      "InlineCode"], " \[LongDash] the antichains at each causal height"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraSlice", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] a causal-height slice or a band of slices"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraSliceQ", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] tests whether a set is a causal-height slice"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell["Measuring constructions", "GuideFunctionsSubsection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraMeasurement", "InlineCode"], " \[LongDash] \
reads cardinalities, lengths, vertex and edge densities on a graph"}], 
   "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["InfraMemberQ", "InlineCode"], 
     " \[LongDash] tests membership in a construction"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell["Spatial reconstruction", "GuideFunctionsSubsection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"", StyleBox["CausalFoliationQ", "InlineCode"], " tests an \
ordered partition into antichains, with every causal edge directed toward a \
later slice"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"", StyleBox["CausalSpatialGraphs", "InlineCode"], " \
reconstructs an undirected graph on each slice; returns an association \
indexed from 1"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"Two distinct events are joined when some lowest common \
ancestor lies in the preceding ", StyleBox["\"AncestorDepth\"", 
      "InlineCode"], " slices, with default depth 1. All lowest common \
ancestors are retained; no unique ancestor is assumed. Equivalently, a common \
ancestor lies in that window. At depth 1, the rule joins events sharing a \
parent in the preceding slice. Omitting the foliation uses ", 
     StyleBox["CausalHeightFoliation", "InlineCode"], ". The first slice has \
no reconstructed edges in this finite past-only model."}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell["Relations and transport between slices", "GuideFunctionsSubsection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"", StyleBox["CausalSliceRelation", "InlineCode"], " \
associates each event in slice i with its causally related events in slice j"}\
], "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{"", StyleBox["CausalSliceMap", "InlineCode"], 
     " returns a single-valued association when every image is unique; ", 
     StyleBox["\"SelectImage\"", "InlineCode"], 
     " supplies an explicit selection otherwise"}], "GuideText"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"", StyleBox["CausalSliceKernel", "InlineCode"], " returns \
nested associations of uniform probabilities over each nonempty causal image"}\
], "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[{"The index pair ", 
     StyleBox["{i, j}", "InlineCode"], " specifies the direction: forward \
when i < j, backward when i > j. A foliation alone supplies neither a \
preferred direction of coarse graining nor a canonical choice among several \
images. A missing image prevents a total map or conservative kernel. Selected \
maps need not preserve spatial adjacency or be onto the target slice. \
Independent uniform long-range kernels need not equal compositions of \
adjacent kernels. "}], "GuideText"], Cell["Tech Notes", 
   "GuideTutorialsSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Spatial Coordinatization", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
      ButtonData -> "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/tutorial/SpatialCo\
ordinatization"]}], "GuideTutorial"], Cell["Related Guides", 
   "GuideMoreAboutSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["InfrageometryBranches", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
      ButtonData -> 
       "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/guide/InfrageometryBranches"]}]\
, "GuideMoreAbout"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["InfraTopology", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
      ButtonData -> 
       "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/guide/InfraTopology"]}], 
   "GuideMoreAbout"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["InfraSubstrates", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
      ButtonData -> 
       "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/guide/InfraSubstrates"]}], 
   "GuideMoreAbout"], Cell[CellGroupData[
    {Cell["Metadata", "MetadataSection"], 
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Categorization", "CategorizationSection"], 
        Cell["Guide", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Entity Type"], 
        Cell["WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry", "Categorization", 
         CellLabel -> "Paclet Name"], Cell["WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`", 
